      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Buffers: Raw Bytes in Node",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Buffer is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Fixed-size== chunk of raw bytes; cannot be resized",
                "A `Uint8Array` subclass",
                "Allocated {orange:outside the V8 heap}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create and convert",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Buffer.from('hi', 'utf8')`",
                  "bytes of the string"
                ],
                [
                  "`Buffer.alloc(n)`",
                  "{green:zero-filled}"
                ],
                [
                  "`Buffer.allocUnsafe(n)`",
                  "faster, may hold old memory"
                ],
                [
                  "`buf.toString('utf8'|'hex'|'base64')`",
                  "bytes to string"
                ],
                [
                  "`Buffer.concat([a, b])`",
                  "new buffer, copies"
                ],
                [
                  "`buf.subarray()` / `slice()`",
                  "{red:shares memory}, no copy"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`allocUnsafe`: ==overwrite before use==, or old data leaks",
                "Writing to a slice changes the original",
                "`chunk.toString()` per chunk splits multi-byte characters"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "r.setEncoding('utf8') // or a decoder:",
                "const d = new StringDecoder('utf8')",
                "text += d.write(chunk)"
              ],
              "note": "decoders hold back partial characters"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is allocUnsafe faster?** It skips zero-filling; the risk is leaking old memory",
                "**Does slice copy?** No, it shares memory",
                "**Decode chunks safely?** `setEncoding('utf8')` or `StringDecoder`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Four Stream Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Four Stream Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Stream Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Data moves in ==chunks==, so memory stays **flat** at any size",
                "Streams are ==EventEmitters==",
                "Chunk is a `Buffer`, or a string after `setEncoding()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Four Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Role",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Readable",
                  "source",
                  "`fs.createReadStream`, HTTP request"
                ],
                [
                  "Writable",
                  "sink",
                  "`fs.createWriteStream`, HTTP response"
                ],
                [
                  "Duplex",
                  "read + write, independent",
                  "TCP socket"
                ],
                [
                  "Transform",
                  "Duplex, output from input",
                  "`zlib.createGzip`, crypto"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`r.on('data')` and `'end'` events",
                "`for await (const chunk of r)`",
                "`r.pipe(w)`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{orange:Paused} until a `data` listener, `pipe()` or `resume()` starts ==flowing=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Writable and Transform",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`write(chunk)` returns ==false== when the buffer is full",
                "Then `end()`; listen for `drain`, `finish`, `error`",
                "Custom Transform: `transform(chunk, enc, cb)`, output via `cb(null, out)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const up = new Transform({",
                "  transform(chunk, enc, cb) { cb(null, chunk.toString().toUpperCase()) }",
                "})"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview",
              "text": "Transform **is** a Duplex. ==objectMode== carries any value, not just Buffers, and is an option on every type."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
