    {
      "title": "pipe, pipeline and Backpressure",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "pipe, pipeline and Backpressure",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Backpressure",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slow consumer tells fast producer to ==stop==",
                "`write()` returns `false` → wait for `'drain'`",
                "Threshold is ==highWaterMark== (buffer size)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Stream",
                "highWaterMark default"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Bytes, Node 22+",
                  "**64 KiB**"
                ],
                [
                  "Bytes, Node 21 and earlier",
                  "**16 KiB**"
                ],
                [
                  "`objectMode`",
                  "**16 objects**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. pipe vs pipeline",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "pipe",
                "pipeline"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Backpressure",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Forwards errors",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Destroys streams",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "import { pipeline } from 'node:stream/promises';",
                "await pipeline(",
                "  fs.createReadStream('in.log'),",
                "  zlib.createGzip(),",
                "  fs.createWriteStream('in.log.gz'));"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Callback form: `stream.pipeline(src, ...transforms, dest, cb)`",
                "==Async generator== functions work as middle stages"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Backpressure?** `write()` false → pause, resume on `'drain'`; `pipe` automates it.",
                "**Why pipeline?** `pipe` leaks on error; pipeline forwards and destroys.",
                "**highWaterMark?** Buffer limit before `write()` returns false.",
                "**Ignore false?** Buffer grows unbounded, memory balloons."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prefer pipeline",
              "text": "`pipe()` leaves streams open on failure → leaked file descriptors."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading Files Efficiently",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reading Files Efficiently",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. readFile Loads It All",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`fs.readFile` / `fs.promises.readFile` load the ==whole file== into memory",
                "Fine for {green:small files}",
                "Large files: {red:memory spikes}, may hit the **Buffer size limit**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Chunks and Lines",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default chunk of a file read stream: ==64 KiB==",
                "A larger `highWaterMark` means ==fewer syscalls== on big files",
                "`{ start, end }` reads a ==byte range==",
                "Big JSON: use ==NDJSON==, one object per line"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "// bigger chunks, fewer syscalls",
                "fs.createReadStream(p, { highWaterMark: 256 * 1024, encoding: 'utf8' })",
                "// byte range, a separate option",
                "fs.createReadStream(p, { start: 0, end: 999 })"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const rl = readline.createInterface({",
                "  input: fs.createReadStream(p), crlfDelay: Infinity });",
                "for await (const line of rl) {",
                "  const obj = JSON.parse(line); // one NDJSON row",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "constant memory, one line at a time"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Serve and Copy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Job",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Serve a big file",
                  "`pipeline(fs.createReadStream(p), res)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Copy a file",
                  "`fs.copyFile(src, dest)`, no JS-land buffering"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never `readFile` a big file to serve it. ==Stream== it with **pipeline**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Stream Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Stream Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. pipe() and errors",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pipe()` forwards ==no errors== and destroys nothing",
                "One stage fails, the others stay open: ==file descriptor leak==",
                "Fix: `pipeline()` destroys every stage and rejects once"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { pipeline } = require('node:stream/promises');",
                "try { await pipeline(src, gzip, dest); }",
                "catch (err) { console.error(err); }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Ignored write()",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "If `write()` returns ==false==, wait for `'drain'` before writing more",
                "Ignored in a loop: buffer grows ==without bound==, memory balloons"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { once } = require('node:events');",
                "for (const row of rows) {",
                "  if (!w.write(row)) await once(w, 'drain');",
                "}",
                "w.end();"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors and chunks",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Why",
                "Instead"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'error'` listener late or missing",
                  "Unhandled `'error'` ==crashes the process==",
                  "Attach before data flows"
                ],
                [
                  "`data += chunk`",
                  "Defeats streaming, splits multi-byte characters",
                  "`setEncoding('utf8')` or `Buffer.concat(chunks)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Use ==pipeline==, honour `write()` and `'drain'`, handle `'error'`, never build strings from raw chunks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
